From 890a5c1108a5429c4b40abb6ad66a78f13edb777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 24 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] rdna-boosts: block 14: MMB per-device arch dispatch (fix mixed-arch multi-GPU)

MMB: key per-arch decisions to the running device, not devices[0]

The MMB dequant-weight GEMM keyed every architecture decision (mmb_enabled,
mmb_cfg, mmb_dense_flag, mmb_wtype_mask, mmb_dense_tmask) on
ggml_cuda_info().devices[0].cc -- the primary's compute capability. In a
mixed-arch multi-GPU setup (gfx1100 primary + gfx1030 secondary) the policy
froze at the primary's: the gfx1030 secondary ran RDNA3-tuned WMMA MMB
kernels (mmb_enabled() is false on RDNA2, which has no WMMA) and produced
byte-exact zero output-projection logits (PPL = vocab size), or garbled
tail-layer GEMMs when the output projection sat on the healthy primary.

All six sites now use the current device's cc
(ggml_cuda_info().devices[ggml_cuda_get_device()].cc), the same idiom the
mmq/mmvq dispatch already uses; mmb_cfg() takes per-arch magic statics and
the wtype/dense tmask statics move inside the env-override branch so the
arch policy is resolved per call.

Verified (Qwen3.8-27B Q6_K_XL, gutenberg corpus, 2 GPU -sm layer):
V620-secondary PPL 248320 -> 2.9844 (200KB) and 2.7546 (772KB); V620-primary
unchanged at 2.9983 (200KB) / 2.7697 (772KB); the XTX-primary +
output-on-XTX garble config (PPL 917.54) -> 2.9842.
